    {"card":{"body_bytes":9420,"body_sha256":"ada419468d732bdc0fbc13b692a0b36f9ee2a9560001f2375f0410fbd98dc88f","url":"https://gate.horizonshield.dev/.well-known/agent-card.json"},"card_signature":{"admitted":true,"count":2,"kid":"hs-2026-09","results":[{"alg":"ES256","index":0,"jku":"https://gate.horizonshield.dev/.well-known/jwks.json","kid":"hs-2026-09","verified":true},{"alg":"ES256","index":1,"jku":"https://gate.horizonshield.dev/.well-known/jwks.json","kid":"hs-2026-09","verified":false}]},"does_not_establish":["who operates the host or controls the key","that the key was the host's key at any time other than the walk","anything about the agent's behaviour or responses","that a signature refused here is invalid under another canonical form"],"jwks":{"body_bytes":256,"body_sha256":"692fd49da681cc0d0bda9ad46963fa5f45957a59d10f84998e9b2e4061209d3c","same_host_as_card":true,"url":"https://gate.horizonshield.dev/.well-known/jwks.json"},"purpose":"a2a-card-signature-walk-v1: https://gate.horizonshield.dev/.well-known/agent-card.json","verifier":{"payload":"RFC 8785 over the served card with the top-level signatures member removed","policy":"probity-a2a-s3-retain-v0-provisional","source":"https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence-vectors/blob/9e596fbff7bb29809d38319aebb56f2141923eb2/interop/a2a-s3-retain-2026-10-01/retain_gate.py","source_sha256":"6313158bd50a5b3db15ae5d8cc7f34aca9d5c747f52749ae3f8b668198c12742"},"walked_at":"2026-10-15T22:44:08Z","walker":"https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence-atlas"}

The key is the one pinned in `interop/a2a-card-walk/walk-key.json` at the commit above, and the same key is served at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/probityai/agent-evidence-atlas/main/interop/a2a-card-walk/walk-key.json. Under the ledger's key rule of 2026-10-16, a key served from a repository at raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/<branch> confers the identity github.com/<owner>, here github.com/probityai.

## 3. What the walk found

Signature 0 of the gate's card (kid hs-2026-09, ES256) verifies over RFC 8785 of the served card with only the top-level `signatures` member removed. Signature 1 does not verify over that payload. Signature 1 was made over the form the A2A SDKs check (canonicalizeAgentCard in @a2a-js/sdk 1.1.0, then RFC 8785), which drops fields the SDK does not keep; the gate states this since horizon-shield f45cd370 at /.well-known/agent-card-signatures.json. The walk also showed that this project's own walk client recorded the card's signatures as read, not verified; since f45cd370 it verifies both forms. Both findings are this walker's.

## 4. How it was checked here

From a fresh clone at the commit above: the SHA-256 of `record_canonical` equals the record's `sha`; the Ed25519 signature verifies under the pinned key; the pinned key equals the key in the record and the key served on the main branch; the card and JWKS files match the signed `body_sha256` and `body_bytes`; `record_canonical` is the sorted-key, no-space ASCII JSON of itself. The card served by the gate on 2026-10-19 still hashes to ada419468d732bdc0fbc13b692a0b36f9ee2a9560001f2375f0410fbd98dc88f.

## 5. Consent

The walker asked for exactly this entry, with the bytes unchanged and pointing at that directory at that commit with that key: https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence-vectors/issues/55#issuecomment-6256752388

## 6. What this entry does not establish

What the record itself says it does not: who operates the host or controls the key, that the key was the host's key at any time other than the walk, anything about the agent's behaviour, that a signature refused there is invalid under another canonical form. In addition: that the walker's key is anyone's beyond github.com/probityai. A disagreeing or later walk is a later entry, never an edit of this one.

**The SHA-256 of this document is anchored to the JIDEC ledger and stamped to Bitcoin. After anchoring, this record cannot be altered. Corrections are later entries that cite this one.**
